From: Le Hoang Quyen <lehoangquyen@chromium.org>
Date: Mon, 26 Oct 2026 15:18:56 +0800
Subject: [3.1.4][8078 after .111] [M156] Validate extensions in
 ValidES3ExtensionFormatCombination

FlyWeb: ANGLE 41c5deee450a from the branch-heads/8078 roll 0ca9887568
(f4f835734108..0b547a1161fb), applied on the 3.1.4 ANGLE tree db885a866b.
Same patch-id as upstream (53571bf905).

Original change's description:
> Validate extensions in ValidES3ExtensionFormatCombination
>
> In ValidateTexImageFormatCombination, GetInternalFormatInfo ignores the
> type parameter for sized internal formats like GL_RGB8 and GL_RGB565,
> whose textureSupport is always true in ES 3.0+. For textures created
> with unsized GL_RGB, ValidateTexImageFormatCombination only sees the
> unsized internalFormat (checking only EXT_texture_type_2_10_10_10_REV),
> while the sized internalFormat is checked afterward in the isSubImage
> branch via ValidES3ExtensionFormatCombination.
>
> Because ValidES3ExtensionFormatCombination did not check extension
> state and the explicit extension gate for GL_RGB8/GL_RGB565 with
> GL_UNSIGNED_INT_2_10_10_10_REV_EXT was placed only in the !isSubImage
> branch, glTexSubImage*D allowed this combination without requiring both
> GL_OES_required_internalformat and GL_EXT_texture_type_2_10_10_10_REV.
>
> Move the extension checks into ValidES3ExtensionFormatCombination so
> both image creation and sub-image updates are properly gated.
>
